      "raw": "# EventListener Examples\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "EventListener Examples"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 3,
      "raw": "This folder shows **multiple ways** to use `EventListener` in QML. The project is now buildable and runnable as a standalone example app.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 4,
      "end_line": 4,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 5,
      "end_line": 5,
      "raw": "The example window now follows the full-bleed shell contract: rendering stays full-window, and the demo content is explicitly placed inside `layoutSafeAreaBounds`.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 6,
      "end_line": 6,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "quote",
      "start_line": 7,
      "end_line": 7,
      "raw": "> Note: component name is `EventListener` (spelled as in code).\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000008",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 8,
      "end_line": 8,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
