    {
      "id": "b000019",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 22,
      "end_line": 22,
      "raw": "## Plain-language explanation (non-developers)\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "Plain-language explanation (non-developers)"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000020",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 23,
      "end_line": 23,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000021",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 24,
      "end_line": 26,
      "raw": "Think of `EventListener` as a tiny “ear” you can place inside any UI element.\nWhen the element is clicked, hovered, or a key is pressed, the ear hears it\nand runs a simple action (like showing a message).\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000022",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 27,
      "end_line": 27,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000023",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 28,
      "end_line": 28,
      "raw": "This lets designers attach behavior without changing the original component.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000024",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 29,
      "end_line": 29,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000025",
      "kind": "thematic_break",
      "start_line": 30,
      "end_line": 30,
      "raw": "---\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000026",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 31,
      "end_line": 31,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000027",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 32,
      "end_line": 32,
      "raw": "## 1) Basic click handler on Label\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "1) Basic click handler on Label"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000028",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 33,
      "end_line": 33,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000029",
      "kind": "fenced_code",
      "start_line": 34,
      "end_line": 42,
      "raw": "```qml\nLV.Label {\n    text: \"Click me\"\n    LV.EventListener {\n        trigger: \"clicked\"\n        action: () => console.log(\"Label clicked\")\n    }\n}\n```\n",
      "language": "qml",
      "code": "LV.Label {\n    text: \"Click me\"\n    LV.EventListener {\n        trigger: \"clicked\"\n        action: () => console.log(\"Label clicked\")\n    }\n}\n",
      "closed": true
    },
